      "title": "🟡 CLI push is now connected, but still only a local runtime affordance",
      "description": "## Problem\nRegistering `CliAdapter` fixes the broken async push path, but it does not turn CLI into a durable external channel. `push_message()` still just prints to stdout, which is fine for local/testing workflows but should not be mistaken for a production notification path.\n\n## Fix\n```python\n# Follow-up direction\n# Keep CliAdapter as a local/testing runtime adapter.\n# If CLI ever needs durable async delivery, design that explicitly instead of\n# stretching stdout semantics.\n```\n\n## Rationale\nThis is not a bug in the current fix. It is a boundary reminder so the new working async path is interpreted correctly."
